Original commit body from 35aa48b801b2c5ba2cba1e49d9d6c02c22723e36:

verify-claims withholds a clean taint verdict when a present language has
no sink in the claim's zone (INV-pivam; every built-in zone since
WI-sojok). _sink_zone_gaps counted ANY sink, community rows included.
Haskell's network zone is covered only by community rows
(Network.HTTP.Client.httpLbs / httpBS / ...), so "untrusted input never
reaches the network" on a Haskell repo read `confirmed` by default and
`inconclusive` under --no-default-overlays: the clean verdict rested on
unvouched rows alone. Found by WI-borib (docs/audits/0026).

ADR-0061 ruling 2 decides it: community rows "may add findings, but
never make a verdict cleaner", and a verdict is cleaner whenever it
moves toward `confirmed`; "an I/O row that makes a call count as
examined" is named in the removing column. So:
- _sink_zone_gaps reports community_only_languages: present languages
  whose every sink in the zone is a community row;
- _apply_sink_zone_gap withholds a clean verdict for them as for an
  uncovered language, with its own reason ("only community rows in the
  'network' zone, which may add findings but never make a verdict
  cleaner (ADR-0061 ruling 2)") so the details stay true;
- violated / inconclusive verdicts are untouched, as before: a flow a
  community sink finds still reads `violated` (the adding half).

Reproduced on a two-function Haskell repo: before, default `confirmed`,
--no-default-overlays `inconclusive`; now both `inconclusive`, each
naming its reason; with getLine flowing into httpLbs, `violated` either
way by default. Catalogue-wide, (haskell, network) is the only
(language, zone) pair covered by community rows alone, and the corpus
holds no Haskell repository: no corpus verdict moves.

Tests: test_community_sinks_zone_coverage.py through `verify-claims`
(the filed case; the no-overlay reason; a found flow still violates);
test_sink_zone_gaps.py's stub catalogue now carries `community` as
TaintSink does, plus a unit case for the separate reason. A mutation
dropping the community-only set turns two tests red.

